      "min": 9,
      "duration": 13.0,
      "text": "Client state vs server state.",
      "visual": "compare",
      "left": {
        "title": "Client state",
        "color": "blue",
        "items": [
          "Modal open, filters, drafts",
          "Zustand, Jotai, Redux"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "Server state",
        "color": "green",
        "items": [
          "Data that lives on an API",
          "TanStack Query, SWR"
        ]
      },
      "say": "Two very different kinds of state hide under one name. Client state is things like whether a modal is open. Server state is a cached copy of remote data, and deserves a data-fetching library, not a global store.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-19-state-mgmt/kinds.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "zustand",
      "min": 10,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "Zustand: a tiny store.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "const useCart = create(set => ({",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  items: [],",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "  add: item => set(s => ({",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "    items: [...s.items, item],",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  })),",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "}));",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "text"
        ],
        [
          "const items = useCart(s => s.items);",
          "pink"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Zustand is a tiny store with almost no boilerplate. You create it with state and actions, then components subscribe to just the slice they select, and re-render only when that slice changes.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-19-state-mgmt/zustand.wav"
    },
